#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the seek amount used by the "Custom value" seek step.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:64
msgid ""
"Custom seek value in seconds. This value is used when the custom seek step "
"is selected. Enter a positive number like 5, 10, or 30. Decimals are "
"allowed, for example 2.5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how much one press of the speed keys changes the playing speed.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:68
msgid ""
"Speed step used when increasing or decreasing playback speed. Enter a "
"positive decimal value like 0.025 or 0.1."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how much one press of the volume keys changes the loudness.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:71
msgid ""
"Volume step used when pressing volume up or down. Allowed range is from 1 to "
"20."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses what the player does at the end of a file. It names the
#. three entries in that list, which should read the same here as they do there.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:75
msgid ""
"What happens after a file ends. Advance to the next file moves to the next "
"item in the playlist. Loop the file repeats the same file automatically. Do "
"nothing keeps playback stopped at the end. Possible values: Advance to the "
"next file, Loop the file, or Do nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that carries on from the first file after the last one.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:80
msgid ""
"Wrap to top for multiple files. When enabled and the playlist has more than "
"one file, moving next from the last file goes to the first file, and moving "
"previous from the first file goes to the last file. Advance-at-end uses the "
"same wrapping behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that remembers where each file was stopped.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:84
msgid ""
"Save current position for each file. When enabled, the app stores the "
"current position of files and restores that position when navigating between "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that evens out the loudness and holds back the loudest peaks.
#. "dynaudnorm" and "alimiter" are the names of the filters doing the work and are not translated.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:88
msgid ""
"Enable dynamic normalize and limiter audio filter. When enabled, audio uses "
"dynaudnorm followed by alimiter to reduce clipping at high volume boosts. "
"Disable it to use raw output without this processing."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that plays the left and right channels mixed together.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:92
msgid ""
"Play audio as Mono. When enabled, a mono downmix filter is applied so left "
"and right channels are combined. Disable it to keep the original channel "
"layout."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: Error message shown when the speed step was typed as something other than a number above zero.
#: UI/AudioPreferences.cs:99
msgid "Speed step must be a positive number."
